1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,272
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۞

2
00:00:05,371 --> 00:00:07,593
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۞

3
00:00:07,747 --> 00:00:10,882
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

4
00:00:12,119 --> 00:00:22,595
Rasool Allah ﷺ used to spend long periods of time in Ghaar-e-Hiraa(غار حرا), in the cave of Hiraa(حرا).

5
00:00:23,492 --> 00:00:28,864
One day, he was visited by the angel Jibreel عليه السّلام,

6
00:00:30,016 --> 00:00:35,486
Jibreel عليه السّلام came to Muhammadﷺ in his original form.

7
00:00:36,102 --> 00:00:44,495
So, Muhammadﷺ saw Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) in his angelic form and not in the form of a man,

8
00:00:44,923 --> 00:00:46,816
which he would sometimes see him in.

9
00:00:47,292 --> 00:00:52,373
In the Hadith(حديث) of Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل), the well known Hadith(حديث) of Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) narrated by Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

10
00:00:52,791 --> 00:00:55,307
Jibreel عليه السّلام came in the form of a man.

11
00:00:55,903 --> 00:00:57,339
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) says:

12
00:00:57,698 --> 00:01:02,944
شَدِيدُ سَوَادِ الشَّعْرِ، شَدِيدُ بَيَاضِ الثِّيَابِ، لا يُرَى عَلَيْهِ أَثَرُ السَّفَرِ،

13
00:01:03,324 --> 00:01:11,760
A man with very dark hair and very bright white clothes and we don't see any traces of travel on him.

14
00:01:12,570 --> 00:01:16,853
So, he came in the form of a man but in this particular situation

15
00:01:17,964 --> 00:01:22,175
Jibreel عليه السّلام appeared in his original form and that happened twice.

16
00:01:23,743 --> 00:01:29,359
Jibreel عليه السّلام came to Muhammadﷺ and told him Iqra(إقراء), recite!

17
00:01:30,402 --> 00:01:33,269
Now the word Iqra(إقراء) has two meanings,

18
00:01:33,983 --> 00:01:37,064
one of them is read and the other is recite,

19
00:01:38,711 --> 00:01:41,870
in the situation of Muhammadﷺ, it means recite.

20
00:01:43,319 --> 00:01:46,366
Jibreel عليه السّلام told Muhammadﷺ, Iqra(إقراء),

21
00:01:47,537 --> 00:01:50,589
Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه responded and said:

22
00:01:50,629 --> 00:01:51,647
مَا اَنَا بِقَارِيْ

23
00:01:51,970 --> 00:01:53,097
I cannot read

24
00:01:53,907 --> 00:02:00,916
Jibreel عليه السّلام grabbed Muhammadﷺ and squeezed him, crushed him

25
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:06,104
 and then he released Muhammadﷺ and told him: Iqra(إقراء), recite!.

26
00:02:07,322 --> 00:02:10,866
Muhammadﷺ responded again and said:

27
00:02:10,926 --> 00:02:11,771
مَا اَنَا بِقَارِيْ

28
00:02:11,914 --> 00:02:13,120
I cannot read.

29
00:02:14,087 --> 00:02:20,161
So, Jibreel عليه السّلام held him a second time and pressed him hard,

30
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:23,160
and then released him again and told him: Iqra(إقراء)!.

31
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:25,774
And this happened three times.

32
00:02:26,289 --> 00:02:32,206
Until, Jibreel عليه السّلام eventually recited the first verses of Qur'an.

33
00:02:33,158 --> 00:02:40,076
اِقْرَأْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ۝ خَلَقَ الْإِنْسَانَ مِنْ عَلَقٍ۝

34
00:02:40,597 --> 00:02:51,080
اقْرَأْ وَرَبُّكَ الْأَكْرَمُ۝ الَّذِي عَلَّمَ بِالْقَلَمِ۝ عَلَّمَ الْإِنْسَانَ مَا لَمْ يَعْلَمْ۝

35
00:02:52,051 --> 00:02:54,948
Recite in the name of Your Lord,

36
00:02:55,652 --> 00:02:57,319
اِقْرَأْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ۝

37
00:02:57,397 --> 00:03:01,574
The One, Who created, created man from clot, recite.

38
00:03:02,176 --> 00:03:07,156
اِقْرَأْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ۝ خَلَقَ الْإِنْسَانَ مِنْ عَلَقٍ۝ اقْرَأْ وَرَبُّكَ الْأَكْرَمُ۝

39
00:03:07,434 --> 00:03:10,331
Recite in the name of Your noble Lord,

40
00:03:10,748 --> 00:03:12,478
الَّذِي عَلَّمَ بِالْقَلَمِ۝

41
00:03:12,537 --> 00:03:14,614
The One, Who taught the pen.

42
00:03:14,859 --> 00:03:16,720
عَلَّمَ الْإِنْسَانَ مَا لَمْ يَعْلَمْ۝

43
00:03:16,943 --> 00:03:19,234
THe taught him, what he knew not.

44
00:03:20,627 --> 00:03:26,362
This was the first encounter between Rasool Allah ﷺ and the angel Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل).

45
00:03:27,792 --> 00:03:34,136
The Messenger of Allah, Muhammadﷺ was terrified by that incident.

46
00:03:35,084 --> 00:03:39,079
He went back home and he entered,

47
00:03:40,289 --> 00:03:45,012
and he immediately went to his wife Khadijah رضي الله عنها and said:

48
00:03:45,709 --> 00:03:48,761
زَمِّلُوْنِي زَمِّلُوْنِيْ، دَثِّرُوْنِيْ دَثِّرُوْنِيْ

49
00:03:49,131 --> 00:03:51,620
Wrap me in a garment! wrap me in a garment!.

50
00:03:51,697 --> 00:03:53,225
Rasool Allah ﷺ was shivering,

51
00:03:54,233 --> 00:03:55,657
he was feeling cold.

52
00:03:56,963 --> 00:03:59,793
And he was asking his wife to wrap him up.

53
00:04:01,485 --> 00:04:08,556
Rasool Allah ﷺ, was terrified and afraid because of this incident that happened to him.

54
00:04:09,416 --> 00:04:19,358
Plus, Rasool Allah ﷺ had a dislike to anything that had to do with Jin(جن), and spirits, and sorcery,

55
00:04:20,292 --> 00:04:28,494
and he was afraid that, what happened to him might be similar to what is happening to sorcerers.

56
00:04:29,455 --> 00:04:34,980
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ explained the incident to his wife Khadijah رضي الله عنها.

57
00:04:35,952 --> 00:04:38,352
Khadijah(خديجه) she responded and said:

58
00:04:38,423 --> 00:04:41,679
كَلَّا لَنْ يُخْزِيْكَ اللهُ أَبَدَا

59
00:04:42,399 --> 00:04:47,278
No, Allah سبحانه وتعالى will never forsake you because of your righteousness,

60
00:04:47,343 --> 00:04:50,893
إِنَّكَ تَحْمِلُ الْكَلَّ ، وَتُعِيْنُ عَلى نَوَائِبِ الْحَقَّ

61
00:04:50,965 --> 00:04:56,748
She said, that you support the needy, you help the poor, you are generous towards the guests.

62
00:04:57,732 --> 00:05:06,808
So, because of the prior conduct of Rasool Allah ﷺ, Khadijah رضي الله عنه knew that such a person cannot be forsaken by God.

63
00:05:06,914 --> 00:05:08,975
Allah سبحانه وتعالى will protect you don't worry,

64
00:05:09,372 --> 00:05:11,648
what happened to you cannot be from Satan.

65
00:05:12,997 --> 00:05:16,947
And then she offered to take Muhammadﷺ to her uncle,

66
00:05:16,987 --> 00:05:20,917
or in some narrations, it is her cousin, Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقة بن نوفل).

67
00:05:21,668 --> 00:05:24,447
So, he went to Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقة بن نوفل)

68
00:05:24,506 --> 00:05:29,963
and we mentioned that Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقة بن نوفل) was a man, who became Christian

69
00:05:30,685 --> 00:05:36,609
and he was lettered and he had scrolls from the Bible which he would study.

70
00:05:38,128 --> 00:05:41,751
Khadijah(خديجه) took Muhammadﷺ to Waraqah(ورقه)

71
00:05:42,547 --> 00:05:46,393
and Waraqah(ورقه) asked Muhammadﷺ to explain exactly what happened.

72
00:05:47,301 --> 00:05:49,676
Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقة بن نوفل) responded and said:

73
00:05:50,788 --> 00:05:53,788
that this is An-Namoos Al-Akbar(ألناموس الأكبر),

74
00:05:53,876 --> 00:05:56,717
 An-Namoos Al-Akbar(ألناموس الأكبر) is the greatest Angel Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل),

75
00:05:57,473 --> 00:05:59,331
who descended on Musa(موسى)

76
00:06:00,444 --> 00:06:04,639
Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقة بن نوفل) immediately knew that this is the angel Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل)

77
00:06:05,103 --> 00:06:11,550
and he is revealing to Muhammadﷺ a revelation similar to that, that was given to Musa عليه السّلام

78
00:06:11,634 --> 00:06:14,164
and you can see Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) that Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقة بن نوفل) here

79
00:06:14,361 --> 00:06:18,409
made the correlation between Muhammadﷺ and Musa(موسى) back to what we were saying.

80
00:06:19,178 --> 00:06:22,699
He said this is similar to what was given to Musa عليه السّلام

81
00:06:23,226 --> 00:06:26,495
and then Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقة بن نوفل) said something interesting, he said:

82
00:06:27,419 --> 00:06:33,953
وَ يَالَيْتَنِيْ كُنْتُ فِيْهَا جَدْعًا حِيْنَ يُخْرِجُكَ قَوْمُكَ مِنْ اَرْضِكْ

83
00:06:34,671 --> 00:06:37,037
And I wish that I was young,

84
00:06:37,751 --> 00:06:41,506
when your people will drive you out of your land.

85
00:06:43,124 --> 00:06:46,995
This was a surprise, to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

86
00:06:47,757 --> 00:06:51,067
So, Rasool Allah question Waraqah(ورقه) and said:

87
00:06:51,107 --> 00:06:52,480
أَوَ مُخْرِجِيَ هُمْ ؟

88
00:06:52,952 --> 00:06:55,567
They will drive me out of my land.

89
00:06:56,146 --> 00:06:57,289
How could that happen?

90
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:04,308
And Rasool Allah ﷺ had every right to question what Waraqah(ورقه) was saying because

91
00:07:05,369 --> 00:07:10,557
Muhammadﷺ was the most beloved man, he was the most admired man in Makkah.

92
00:07:11,072 --> 00:07:12,719
How could they drive me out?

93
00:07:13,067 --> 00:07:17,218
Muhammadﷺ belong to the noblest family in Makkah, Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم).

94
00:07:17,837 --> 00:07:23,625
Muhammadﷺ was someone, who had no quarrels with the people,

95
00:07:23,875 --> 00:07:26,369
for them to drive him out of his land.

96
00:07:26,634 --> 00:07:30,573
Plus, they were living in the environment, and the culture,

97
00:07:31,018 --> 00:07:35,868
which it was unacceptable to drive somebody out of their homeland.

98
00:07:36,058 --> 00:07:42,802
In the tribal society, the only way they could survive in the harsh environment of the desert

99
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:45,978
is for them to hold together.

100
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:49,554
So, you had extreme loyalty to the tribe,

101
00:07:50,510 --> 00:07:55,587
every member of a tribe considered that their total loyalty goes to the tribe,

102
00:07:55,971 --> 00:07:59,436
and the same thing the tribe is loyal to the member of the tribe.

103
00:08:00,070 --> 00:08:04,404
Anything else would mean death, in that harsh environment,

104
00:08:04,490 --> 00:08:10,141
so they used to stick together, and their family relationships were very strong.

105
00:08:10,858 --> 00:08:15,465
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was asking, Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقة بن نوفل) would they drive me out of my land.?

106
00:08:15,522 --> 00:08:16,746
Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقة بن نوفل) said:

107
00:08:17,763 --> 00:08:22,348
"Anyone who has presented his people with something similar to this,

108
00:08:22,981 --> 00:08:27,441
would be driven out of their land, they will take him as an enemy."

109
00:08:28,221 --> 00:08:32,143
Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقة بن نوفل) was a wise man, who studied history.

110
00:08:32,519 --> 00:08:36,537
And he knows the nature of the conflict between truth and falsehood.

111
00:08:37,083 --> 00:08:40,668
He knew that even though Muhammadﷺ was admired by his people,

112
00:08:40,808 --> 00:08:43,352
even though he belonged to the most noble family,

113
00:08:43,823 --> 00:08:49,737
even though he had no conflicts with the members of his community.

114
00:08:50,395 --> 00:08:54,132
But because he is calling them to Islam,

115
00:08:54,776 --> 00:08:56,277
this is what will happen to him.

116
00:08:56,685 --> 00:09:02,624
He will go through these trials and tribulations and what Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقة بن نوفل) said, came to fruition.

117
00:09:02,950 --> 00:09:05,541
It happened exactly as he stated.

118
00:09:06,069 --> 00:09:13,701
And the words of Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقة بن نوفل) were an early warning for Muhammadﷺ to tell him, what was coming ahead,

119
00:09:14,074 --> 00:09:18,232
that it's going to be difficult, and it won't be easy for you.

120
00:09:20,115 --> 00:09:25,928
We talked about the revelation, the beginning of the revelation, Al-Wahee(ألوحى).

121
00:09:27,190 --> 00:09:34,429
And the first words that were given to Rasool Allah ﷺ were Iqraa(إقراء), recite.

122
00:09:36,174 --> 00:09:39,722
What does that mean for us? Iqraa(إقراء),

123
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:44,267
these words, Iqraa(إقراء), what they mean to us,

124
00:09:44,687 --> 00:09:49,732
the Muslims is that we are an Ummah(امة) that reads,

125
00:09:50,472 --> 00:09:54,297
an Ummah(امة) that studies and Ummah(امة) that learns.

126
00:09:56,208 --> 00:10:01,350
These words had the powerful effect on an illiterate nation, that made them the scholars of the world.

127
00:10:03,326 --> 00:10:10,024
When Qur'an was revealed, the followers of Rasool Allah ﷺ were mostly illiterate.

128
00:10:10,970 --> 00:10:15,776
But these words inspired them to learn.

129
00:10:17,205 --> 00:10:19,397
And within a very short time,

130
00:10:20,095 --> 00:10:26,159
the Muslim Ummah(امة) was the most educated, the most scholarly nation on the face of the earth.

131
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:32,713
And the number of scholars that this Ummah(امة) has produced, is unsurpassed.

132
00:10:34,490 --> 00:10:39,263
And when you look at the qualities of the scholars of this Ummah(امة), you see their uniqueness

133
00:10:39,871 --> 00:10:45,292
and the fact that they don't have any resemblance in any other nation.

134
00:10:46,189 --> 00:10:48,538
Take, for example, the memory of Al-Bukhari(ألبخاري),

135
00:10:50,127 --> 00:10:53,863
his ability to memorize over a quarter of a million Hadith(حديث)

136
00:10:54,998 --> 00:11:00,845
or Shafi(الشافعي), who said that when I open a book, I have to cover one page,

137
00:11:01,186 --> 00:11:07,772
because I would memorize everything, I don't want the information on the two pages to mix, photographic memory.

138
00:11:08,914 --> 00:11:16,224
Or the scholar Al-Wafaa Bin Aqeel(أبوالوفاء بن عقيل), who wrote an encyclopedia of 300 volumes unfortunately,

139
00:11:16,379 --> 00:11:19,950
it didn't survive, the original copies of it were

140
00:11:20,206 --> 00:11:24,094
in the library of Baghdad(بغداد), which was sacked by the Tataar(تتار),

141
00:11:25,156 --> 00:11:27,616
only I think a volume or two survived.

142
00:11:28,413 --> 00:11:34,011
It was the power of these words, Iqraa(إقراء) that made this Sudden change in the Ummah(امة).

143
00:11:35,685 --> 00:11:41,052
Now, with Rasool Allah ﷺ the situation is different

144
00:11:41,376 --> 00:11:48,387
with Rasool Allah ﷺ he did not learn how to read and write.

145
00:11:50,014 --> 00:11:53,189
With Rasool Allah ﷺ the word meant, recite.

146
00:11:53,498 --> 00:11:57,338
For us it means that we have to learn how to read and write.

147
00:11:58,369 --> 00:12:02,309
But for Rasool Allah ﷺ, it has a different meaning, it has the meaning of

148
00:12:02,402 --> 00:12:06,111
reciting and repeating what Allahسبحانه وتعالى has revealed to him...

149
00:12:06,695 --> 00:12:07,253
Why.?

150
00:12:07,632 --> 00:12:12,772
Because with Rasool Allah ﷺ, Allah wanted him to be illiterate

151
00:12:13,820 --> 00:12:17,643
it was part of the plan, the decree of Allahعَزّ وجَلّ,

152
00:12:18,350 --> 00:12:19,842
Allahسبحانه وتعالى says:

153
00:12:20,273 --> 00:12:33,396
وَمَا كُنْتَ تَتْلُو مِنْ قَبْلِهِ مِنْ كِتَابٍ وَلَا تَخُطُّهُ بِيَمِينِكَ ۖ إِذًا لَارْتَابَ الْمُبْطِلُونَ۝

154
00:12:34,064 --> 00:12:39,169
If you had known scripture before this,

155
00:12:39,486 --> 00:12:43,423
or were able to write, then this would cause doubts

156
00:12:43,629 --> 00:12:45,402
in the ones, who want to make doubts.

157
00:12:45,970 --> 00:12:52,766
So, Allahسبحانه وتعالى says that Muhammadﷺ, first of all, he did not learn any scripture before Qur'an

158
00:12:53,368 --> 00:12:57,039
and he had not learned the ability to read and write,

159
00:12:58,829 --> 00:12:59,948
so he was illiterate.

160
00:13:00,702 --> 00:13:06,821
Now why would Rasool Allah ﷺ after Islam have to learn to read and write

161
00:13:07,266 --> 00:13:10,745
What purpose would that serve him, what good would that do for him?

162
00:13:11,037 --> 00:13:15,075
When he is receiving the knowledge fresh from Allah سبحانه وتعالى through Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل).

163
00:13:16,302 --> 00:13:19,949
What purpose would it be for Rasool Allah ﷺ to learn how to read and write.

164
00:13:20,397 --> 00:13:26,616
For us, reading is our key to knowledge that's how we can learn knowledge

165
00:13:27,068 --> 00:13:30,616
but for Rasool Allah ﷺ he was been taught by Jibreel عليه السّلام.

166
00:13:32,519 --> 00:13:36,541
And there's nothing that books will do for Rasool Allah ﷺ,

167
00:13:37,041 --> 00:13:42,571
there is no knowledge that the books can offer to Rasool Allah ﷺ when, he is receiving the knowledge directly from Allah.

168
00:13:43,912 --> 00:13:46,817
So, Iqraa(اِقراء)  has a different meaning for Muhammadﷺ.

169
00:13:47,198 --> 00:13:52,014
It means recite in his case, but for us, it means read.

170
00:13:52,656 --> 00:13:58,339
And this is how the early Muslims understood the first word that was revealed in Qur'an.

171
00:13:58,643 --> 00:14:01,745
And notice that in the fourth Ayah(آية):

172
00:14:02,465 --> 00:14:08,150
