00:43:39,534 --> 00:43:41,726
Therefore he was brought up on Islam from day one.

549
00:43:42,781 --> 00:43:45,741
Because again, he was adopted by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

550
00:43:46,082 --> 00:43:51,841
Therefore, we would say that the first man to become Muslim was Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه.

551
00:43:52,541 --> 00:43:56,906
Now let's continue with the quotation from Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر), he says,

552
00:43:57,421 --> 00:43:59,688
combining these accounts, we see

553
00:43:59,986 --> 00:44:03,380
that Khadijah(خديجه) was the first woman to accept Islam,

554
00:44:03,580 --> 00:44:08,520
the leader of the pack, as it were, and also she proceeded the men.

555
00:44:08,981 --> 00:44:13,177
Among the slaves, the first to accept Islam was Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه),

556
00:44:13,772 --> 00:44:18,176
by the way Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) was also in the household of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

557
00:44:19,215 --> 00:44:22,509
And the first boy to accept Islam was Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب),

558
00:44:22,863 --> 00:44:28,556
he was young then, and had not reached the age of puberty, as generally believed.

559
00:44:28,977 --> 00:44:32,421
 These were the family of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

560
00:44:33,093 --> 00:44:37,218
The first free man to accept Islam was Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), the trusting,

561
00:44:37,695 --> 00:44:43,351
his conversion was more beneficial than that of those mentioned before,

562
00:44:43,622 --> 00:44:46,915
because he was highly a respected leader,

563
00:44:47,200 --> 00:44:50,573
and honored chief of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and the man of wealth.

564
00:44:51,161 --> 00:44:53,701
He became a missionary for Islam,

565
00:44:53,929 --> 00:45:00,022
and was very much liked and admired for spending his wealth in the service of Allah and His messenger.

566
00:45:01,036 --> 00:45:04,730
So, it's an interesting note from Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر),

567
00:45:05,000 --> 00:45:08,428
that Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) was the most beneficial.

568
00:45:08,918 --> 00:45:09,454
Why?

569
00:45:09,494 --> 00:45:14,504
Because he was a wealthy, prominent member of the society,

570
00:45:14,897 --> 00:45:18,331
who brought in, all of his resources for the service of Islam.

571
00:45:19,337 --> 00:45:23,433
See, when you say wealthy and respected member of the society, it would mean nothing.

572
00:45:23,850 --> 00:45:29,645
if a person does not bring in, what Allah has endowed them with, to serve Islam

573
00:45:29,698 --> 00:45:32,851
 but Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه, he put everything on the line.

574
00:45:33,252 --> 00:45:36,546
All of his wealth, all of his business, his connections, his knowledge,

575
00:45:36,757 --> 00:45:38,780
he used it all for Islam.

576
00:45:39,144 --> 00:45:42,795
He put everything under the service of Rasool Allah ﷺ, it's all yours.

577
00:45:43,287 --> 00:45:46,108
And that's why it was called Siddique(الصديق) because it was the first

578
00:45:47,121 --> 00:45:48,886
Siddique(الصديق) is the one, who believes

579
00:45:49,645 --> 00:45:52,616
people rejected Rasool Allah ﷺ Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) accepted him.

580
00:45:53,217 --> 00:45:59,133
There was a saying that everyone hesitated in accepting Islam, except Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

581
00:45:59,482 --> 00:46:02,295
 as soon as this was presented to him, he accepted it

582
00:46:03,141 --> 00:46:08,572
Everyone else thought about it, gave it a second thought with Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), it was an immediate response.

583
00:46:09,218 --> 00:46:15,634
And he would never have second thoughts about serving Islam he would, he was the one, who came with all of his wealth,

584
00:46:16,030 --> 00:46:18,810
he was the one, who first believed in Rasool Allah ﷺ in Makkah,

585
00:46:19,047 --> 00:46:21,610
he was the one, who first believed in Al-Israa Wal Miraj(الاسراء والمعراج)

586
00:46:21,845 --> 00:46:25,450
He was the one or accompanied Rasool Allah ﷺ in difficult journey of Al-Hijrah(هجرة

587
00:46:26,793 --> 00:46:29,471
That was the status of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

588
00:46:32,112 --> 00:46:39,709
We talked earlier about the loyalty of Rasool Allah ﷺ to the ones, who stood with him, in the early days.

589
00:46:40,042 --> 00:46:41,933
Here we have a Hadith(حديث) in Bukhari(بخاريْ):

590
00:46:43,009 --> 00:46:46,827
Abu Darda(ابو درداء) narrates that feud happened between Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر) ,

591
00:46:47,302 --> 00:46:51,438
now these were the two advisors of Rasool Allah ﷺ, they're very close to him.

592
00:46:52,011 --> 00:46:53,752
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said:

593
00:46:54,112 --> 00:46:57,191
I would see Rasool Allah ﷺ enter with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر),

594
00:46:57,331 --> 00:46:59,123
he would leave with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر),

595
00:46:59,337 --> 00:47:01,036
he would sit with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر)

596
00:47:01,565 --> 00:47:05,545
where ever you would see Rasool Allah ﷺ you would see Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) on one side and Umar(عُمَر) on the other,

597
00:47:05,618 --> 00:47:07,515
these were his two advisors.

598
00:47:08,791 --> 00:47:14,270
But still Rasool Allah ﷺ had this special loyalty to the ones,

599
00:47:14,836 --> 00:47:17,324
who were with him from the early days.

600
00:47:18,371 --> 00:47:20,981
So, this dispute happened between Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر),

601
00:47:21,422 --> 00:47:23,022
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

602
00:47:23,453 --> 00:47:25,335
Allah sent me to you

603
00:47:25,597 --> 00:47:31,132
and all of you said, You lie, except Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), who said, he spoke the truth.

604
00:47:31,642 --> 00:47:34,488
And he dedicated himself and his fortune to me.

605
00:47:35,173 --> 00:47:39,848
Will you then leave this friend of mine to me, he said that twice.

606
00:47:40,348 --> 00:47:42,020
He said leave my friend alone.

607
00:47:42,325 --> 00:47:44,262
Don't harm him, leave him alone.

608
00:47:46,426 --> 00:47:54,738
The early stage of Da'wah(دعوة); the secret stage was over, with the revelation of the verse.

609
00:47:55,463 --> 00:47:59,560
وَأَنْذِرْ عَشِيرَتَكَ الْأَقْرَبِينَ۝

610
00:48:00,347 --> 00:48:03,430
Warn your nearest Kindred.

611
00:48:04,289 --> 00:48:05,682
This is in Surah Ash-Shua'raa(سورة الشعرآء)

612
00:48:06,254 --> 00:48:08,077
it was revealed to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

613
00:48:08,611 --> 00:48:12,042
Rasool Allah ﷺ went out and stood on the mountain of As-Saffah(ألصفاء).

614
00:48:12,635 --> 00:48:13,494
And he called;

615
00:48:13,574 --> 00:48:15,456
وا صَبَاحَاه

616
00:48:16,175 --> 00:48:21,283
Wa'Sub-haa(وا صَبَاحَاهْ) is like, sounding the alarm, the sirens.

617
00:48:22,289 --> 00:48:27,953
You don't say Wa'Sub-haa(وا صَبَاحَاهْ), unless there's an emergency going on, there's something very critical.

618
00:48:28,774 --> 00:48:34,303
So, everyone who heard Rasool Allah ﷺ

619
00:48:35,095 --> 00:48:39,025
ran towards the source of the voice.

620
00:48:39,708 --> 00:48:44,303
And the ones, who could not go with send someone to report back to them.

621
00:48:45,343 --> 00:48:49,250
So, Wa'Sub-haa(وا صَبَاحَاهْ) is something that you don't say unless it's something very important.

622
00:48:49,788 --> 00:48:51,163
So, all of the people gathered,

623
00:48:52,620 --> 00:48:54,445
Rasool Allah ﷺ asked them,

624
00:48:55,414 --> 00:49:01,986
if I tell you that there is an army behind this mountain that is about to ambush you, attack you.

625
00:49:02,451 --> 00:49:03,834
Would you believe me?,

626
00:49:04,408 --> 00:49:05,063
They said:

627
00:49:05,372 --> 00:49:07,936
مَا عَهِدْنَا عَلَيْكَ كَذِبَا

628
00:49:08,538 --> 00:49:10,866
we have never heard you lie.

629
00:49:12,570 --> 00:49:14,040
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

630
00:49:14,143 --> 00:49:17,628
فَاِنِّيْ نَذِيْرُلَّكُمْ بَيْنَ يَدَيْ عَذَابٍ اَلِيْمْ

631
00:49:18,119 --> 00:49:21,729
I am here to warn you a severe punishment.

632
00:49:22,472 --> 00:49:26,776
I came to warn you, Allah سبحانه وتعالى sent me as a Warner to you,

633
00:49:27,129 --> 00:49:31,012
and I'm warning you as severe punishment that will befall you if you don't believe.

634
00:49:32,137 --> 00:49:39,576
These were the words Rasool Allah ﷺ chose to deliver in his first public speech to the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

635
00:49:39,926 --> 00:49:41,831
I am here to warn you.

636
00:49:42,040 --> 00:49:45,154
So, you can see that it was very straightforward.

637
00:49:45,516 --> 00:49:48,966
Without much introduction, straight to the point.

638
00:49:49,441 --> 00:49:52,176
I am warning you a severe punishment.

639
00:49:52,877 --> 00:49:57,057
Rasool Allah ﷺ did that because the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء),

640
00:49:57,710 --> 00:50:02,446
Allah سبحانه وتعالى tells them that your duty is Balaagh Mubeen(بلاغ مبين),

641
00:50:02,843 --> 00:50:05,340
your duty is to convey the message plainly.

642
00:50:06,160 --> 00:50:09,534
So, when you convey the message, it should not be confusing.

643
00:50:09,902 --> 00:50:15,102
It should not be obscure, it should not be sugar coated, it should not be altered, it should be straightforward.

644
00:50:15,415 --> 00:50:18,431
Because you don't want to leave any doubts in the mind of the listener,

645
00:50:18,698 --> 00:50:19,787
you don't want to confuse them.

646
00:50:20,033 --> 00:50:23,548
Now unfortunately, many times when we make Da'wah(دعوة) we confuse the listener

647
00:50:24,144 --> 00:50:26,829
the listener comes out not knowing what's going on.

648
00:50:27,112 --> 00:50:28,200
What are we talking about?

649
00:50:28,429 --> 00:50:30,295
What are the consequences of belief?

650
00:50:30,475 --> 00:50:32,311
And what are the consequences of disbelief?

651
00:50:32,684 --> 00:50:35,776
But Rasool Allah ﷺ would leave no doubt in the mind of the listener.

652
00:50:36,235 --> 00:50:41,048
The listener would know that if they believe they will be a promised Jannah(جنة).

653
00:50:41,208 --> 00:50:43,626
And if they don't, they're risking hellfire.

654
00:50:44,931 --> 00:50:48,264
They know that the consequences of disbelief would be hellfire.

655
00:50:49,031 --> 00:50:53,470
And Rasool Allah ﷺ would make his warnings very straightforward.

656
00:50:53,899 --> 00:51:01,926
Now, Rasool Allah ﷺ called the people and the people assumed that, this is something urgent and important, and it was.!!

657
00:51:03,212 --> 00:51:04,995
Abu Lahab(ابو لهب) responded and said:

658
00:51:06,045 --> 00:51:08,593
تَبَّنْ الَّكَ اَلِى هَذَا جَمَاعْتَنَا

659
00:51:09,284 --> 00:51:11,915
May evil befall you the rest of your day.

660
00:51:11,955 --> 00:51:13,552
Is this why you called us.?

661
00:51:15,014 --> 00:51:16,926
Abu Lahab(ابو لهب) was upset, he was angry.

662
00:51:17,861 --> 00:51:18,702
Why?

663
00:51:18,829 --> 00:51:27,281
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ called for an urgent gathering during the official business hours,

664
00:51:27,503 --> 00:51:29,828
and he took me from my work and my business,

665
00:51:30,096 --> 00:51:34,010
and I came here not to hear something serious, according to Abu Lahab(ابو لهب).

666
00:51:34,942 --> 00:51:39,107
He was talking about afterlife, he's talking about religion,

667
00:51:39,201 --> 00:51:41,767
he's talking about spirituality.

668
00:51:42,540 --> 00:51:46,085
He's talking about things that are not tangible

669
00:51:46,905 --> 00:51:48,288
He's wasting my time,

670
00:51:48,580 --> 00:51:53,175
I could have made money, during those valuable minutes that I spent listening to him.

671
00:51:54,252 --> 00:51:55,786
So, Abu Lahab(ابو لهب) was upset.

672
00:51:57,154 --> 00:52:01,409
Abu Lahab(ابو لهب) is thinking that this is the material world, this is real world

673
00:52:01,772 --> 00:52:06,831
And if you don't have a deal to discuss some business, some money to make, don't waste my time.

674
00:52:08,263 --> 00:52:08,854
And he said,

675
00:52:08,894 --> 00:52:10,076
تَبَّاً الَّكَ سَائِرَ الْيَوْمْ

676
00:52:10,152 --> 00:52:12,890
may evil befall you the rest of the day, you wasted my time.

677
00:52:13,801 --> 00:52:18,825
Abu Lahab(ابو لهب) is not alone, in that he's speaking on behalf of a lot of people.

678
00:52:20,270 --> 00:52:21,823
People don't want to listen about religion,

679
00:52:21,863 --> 00:52:24,771
don't waste my time talking about this religious stuff.

680
00:52:25,804 --> 00:52:27,497
If you can promise me some money,

681
00:52:27,725 --> 00:52:30,594
if they can promise me something that will do me good in this world,

682
00:52:30,765 --> 00:52:32,100
otherwise, don't waste my time.

683
00:52:32,405 --> 00:52:35,512
Excuse me, sir, can I talk to you about religion for half an hour?

684
00:52:35,765 --> 00:52:36,694
No, I'm busy.

685
00:52:36,768 --> 00:52:38,633
I can't afford half an hour.

686
00:52:38,934 --> 00:52:40,921
And then what is that man in a rush to do?

687
00:52:41,661 --> 00:52:44,666
Maybe is going to buy a refrigerator or a car or something

688
00:52:45,097 --> 00:52:51,835
you know, you're asking the person to give you half an hour from their time to talk about their salvation and they would refuse,

689
00:52:52,172 --> 00:52:57,470
 nevertheless, they willing to spend hours and hours before buying your refrigerator or an oven.

690
00:52:59,243 --> 00:53:00,698
They would look at all of the deals,

691
00:53:01,174 --> 00:53:03,211
they would visit all of the department stores.

692
00:53:03,926 --> 00:53:10,328
Before a person would buy a used car, they would spend days and days of research they would go and consult the blue book.

693
00:53:10,883 --> 00:53:14,878
So, I would consult the blue book then I would go and read all of the classified ads

694
00:53:15,270 --> 00:53:20,381
days and days of my valuable life, I'm spending just to save a few hundred dollars.

695
00:53:21,201 --> 00:53:27,135
and I'm not willing to give half an hour of my time to learn about what will save me, in my eternal life.

696
00:53:28,682 --> 00:53:31,817
So, Abu Lahab(ابو لهب) was representing lots of people when they said:

697
00:53:31,841 --> 00:53:33,454
تَبَّاً الَّكَ سَائِرَ الْيَوْمْ

698
00:53:34,468 --> 00:53:37,088
Allah سبحانه وتعالى revealed the Surah(سورة).

699
00:53:37,537 --> 00:53:48,622
تَبَّتْ يَدَا أَبِي لَهَبٍ وَتَبَّ۝ مَا أَغْنَىٰ عَنْهُ مَالُهُ وَمَا كَسَبَ۝

700
00:53:49,296 --> 00:53:55,009
The hands of Abu Lahab(ابواهب) will perish and perish he and then the Ayah(آية) says:

701
00:53:55,034 --> 00:53:57,998
مَا أَغْنَىٰ عَنْهُ مَالُهُ وَمَا كَسَبَ۝

702
00:53:58,546 --> 00:54:01,584
His wealth will not do him any good.

703
00:54:02,338 --> 00:54:06,623
What was keeping Abu Lahab(ابو لهب) away from the truth, business, his wealth.

704
00:54:07,137 --> 00:54:11,643
Allah سبحانه وتعالى is saying that his wealth will do him no good.

705
00:54:13,282 --> 00:54:16,842
The people who are rushing after Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) will do the no good.

706
00:54:17,369 --> 00:54:18,849
If they don't have Islam in their heart.

707
00:54:20,261 --> 00:54:22,351
This Surah(سورة) is a miracle of Qur'an

708
00:54:23,902 --> 00:54:27,500
because it says that Abu Lahab(ابولهب) and his wife are in hellfire.

709
00:54:29,284 --> 00:54:34,628
And this Ayah(آية) was revealed while Abu Lahab(ابولهب) and his wife were still alive.

710
00:54:35,370 --> 00:54:40,440
If Abu Lahab(ابولهب) and his wife wanted to prove Qur'an wrong, they could have said we are Muslims.

711
00:54:41,343 --> 00:54:44,332
But they remained disbelievers until, the day they died.

712
00:54:44,853 --> 00:54:47,314
So, this is a miracle of Qur'an.

713
00:54:47,738 --> 00:54:50,850
It is speaking about an event that did not happen yet.

714
00:54:51,544 --> 00:54:55,479
It is saying that Abu Lahab(ابولهب) and his wife are in Hellfire, while they're still alive.

715
00:54:56,061 --> 00:54:59,160
And they could have embraced Islam if they wanted to prove Qur'an wrong.

716
00:54:59,582 --> 00:55:00,429
But they didn't do it.

717
00:55:02,040 --> 00:55:05,167
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

